468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (This is perhaps the easiest hardware project you can design using your Raspberry Pi. In this project, you will connect an LED to one of the ports of the Raspberry Pi and then flash the LED once a second. The aim of this project is to show how a simple Python program can be written and then run from a file. The project also shows how to connect an LED to a Raspberry Pi GPIO pin. In addition, the project shows how to use the GPIO library to configure and set a GPIO pin to logic 0 or 1. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
